---
import '../styles/site.css';
import canopyIcon from '../assets/canopy-icon-192.png';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
const image = (name) => `${base}images/${name}`;
---
<html lang="en">
  <head><meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" /><meta name="description" content="A local-first workspace that turns OpenCode agents into a coordinated, accountable team." /><title>Canopy | Your agents. Your machine. Your momentum.</title></head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href={base} aria-label="Canopy home"><img class="brand-mark" src={canopyIcon.src} width="28" height="28" alt="" /> Canopy</a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="nav">Menu</button><nav id="nav"><a href={`${base}docs/`}>Docs</a><a href="https://github.com/tiki51/canopy">GitHub</a><a class="button small" href={`${base}getting-started/`}>Get started</a></nav></header>
    <main id="main">
        <section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">LOCAL-FIRST AGENT WORKSPACE</p><h1>Your agents.<br /><em>Your machine.</em><br />Your momentum.</h1><p class="lede">Give your OpenCode agents names, roles, and focused channels. They coordinate the work, hand tasks off, and leave a record you can review.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`${base}getting-started/`}>Run your first Canopy task in 5 minutes <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/tiki51/canopy">View on GitHub ↗</a></div><p class="trust">Open source <b>·</b> Runs locally <b>·</b> Agents run on OpenCode</p></div><figure class="hero-shot"><div class="live"><i></i> channel view</div><img src={image('channel-conversation-dark.png')} alt="Canopy channel #payment-retries: Priya asks @backend for a root cause; findings and a delegation follow." /><figcaption>#payment-retries · one task, start to finish</figcaption></figure></section>
        <section class="workflow wrap"><p class="eyebrow">THE WORKFLOW</p><h2>Work moves. The record stays.</h2><div class="timeline"><article><span>01</span><h3>Give the work a room</h3><p>One channel. One outcome.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Name an owner</h3><p>A named owner starts it.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Bring in specialists</h3><p>Delegate or hand off with the record available.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Review what happened</h3><p>Decisions, activity, and spend stay with the work.</p></article></div></section>
        <section class="proof wrap"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">PROOF, NOT PROMISES</p><h2>Stay close to the work.</h2></div><div class="proof-row"><img src={image('agent-working-dark.png')} width="1440" height="900" alt="Canopy showing an agent actively working in a channel" /><div><p class="kicker">01 / ACTIVITY</p><h3>Watch the work, not a spinner</h3><p>Ownership, status, and every turn land in the channel. Each finished line says what ran, what it cost, and how long it took.</p><ul class="proof-list"><li><h4>Live task status</h4><p>The channel records the task's owner, state, and result, so the next decision starts with context.</p></li><li><h4>Visible agent ownership</h4><p>Each task has a named owner. Delegations and handoffs make changes in responsibility visible in the record.</p></li><li><h4>Activity you can audit</h4><p>Messages, tool activity, and finished turns stay together, including what ran, how long it took, and reported cost.</p></li></ul></div></div><div class="proof-row reverse"><img src={image('agent-page-dark.png')} width="1440" height="900" alt="Canopy agent page with role and persistent memory" /><div><p class="kicker">02 / MEMORY</p><h3>A team that remembers</h3><p>Agents have names, roles, and a memory that travels with them. What one learns in a channel, it knows in the next — so agents carry learned preferences into their next task.</p><ul class="proof-list"><li><h4>Persistent agent memory</h4><p>Agents can retain learned preferences and working context, rather than starting every task from zero.</p></li><li><h4>Role-aware collaboration</h4><p>Give agents clear roles, then bring the right specialist into the channel when the work calls for it.</p></li><li><h4>Shared channel history</h4><p>The channel keeps the conversation and decisions in one place, so handoffs begin with the record intact.</p></li></ul></div></div><div class="proof-row"><img src={image('costs-dark.png')} width="1440" height="1780" alt="Canopy costs page showing budget and usage controls" /><div><p class="kicker">03 / CONTROL</p><h3>Autonomy with brakes</h3><p>Set limits before work begins. Spend is visible per channel, and when a channel hits its limit, its agents go quiet until you raise it.</p><ul class="proof-list"><li><h4>Per-channel budgets</h4><p>Set a dollar limit when you create a channel, or adjust it later from the Budget panel.</p></li><li><h4>Transparent usage</h4><p>See spend by channel, agent, model, and trigger, plus the turns that cost the most.</p></li><li><h4>Nothing resumes without you</h4><p>At the limit, new wake-ups are dropped. Raise or remove the limit when you are ready; a turn already running is allowed to finish.</p></li></ul></div></div></section>
       <section class="architecture wrap"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVATE WORK. SHARED COORDINATION.</p><p class="architecture-lede">OpenCode executes privately; Canopy coordinates visibly.</p><div class="diagram"><div>OpenCode session</div><b>→</b><div>Canopy coordination</div><b>→</b><div>Channel record</div></div></section>
        <section class="closing wrap"><h2>Build with a team that stays on your machine.</h2><p>Open-source coordination for the agents you already run.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`${base}getting-started/`}>Get started <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}docs/`}>Read the docs</a></div></section>
    </main>
      <footer class="wrap footer"><span class="brand"><img class="brand-mark" src={canopyIcon.src} width="28" height="28" alt="" /> Canopy</span><div><a href={`${base}docs/`}>Docs</a><a href="https://github.com/tiki51/canopy">GitHub</a><a href="https://opencode.ai">OpenCode</a><a href="https://github.com/tiki51/canopy-site/blob/main/LICENSE">License</a></div></footer>
     <script>const b=document.querySelector('.menu-toggle'),n=document.querySelector('#nav'),links=n?.querySelectorAll('a');const close=()=>{b?.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');n?.classList.remove('open')};b?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const open=b.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true';if(open){close();return}b.setAttribute('aria-expanded','true');n?.classList.add('open');links?.[0]?.focus()});document.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{if(event.key==='Escape'&&b?.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'){close();b.focus()}});</script>
  </body>
</html>
